# Project SUTRA — Enforced Agent Rules & Learned User Directives

### 🛡️ Rule 001: Team Member Role Clarifications & Scope
- **Harika**: Assigned exclusively to Subsystem E (Research Synthesis, Technical Documentation, Verification Gate Metric Audits G1-G6, Presentation Decks & Flight Logs). DO NOT assign complex low-level C++/ROS2 coding or Gazebo plugin writing to Harika.
- **Nikhil**: Tech Architect & Subsystem B Lead (Swarm Comms Mesh, Deep JSCC Neural Coding, Gazebo Sim Ops).
- **Rohith Kumar**: Subsystem A Lead (Autonomous Navigation, GNC, PX4 Offboard Mode, ORCA Avoidance).
- **Vedanth Sai Ram**: Subsystem C Lead (Tri-Modal AI Perception, YOLOv8 TensorRT, Target Geolocation).
- **Siva Kesava**: Subsystem D Lead (3D GIS Dashboard, React + Mapbox GL JS, WebGPU HUD, Emergency RTL).

### 🛡️ Rule 002: Simulation Engine & Active Hardware Fleet
- **Primary Standalone Simulator Machine**: **ASUS TUF A15 (RTX 3050 4GB VRAM)**. Works 100% standalone! Gazebo Sim 8 (Jazzy) + Ogre2 PBR footprint is < 350 MB VRAM, leaving > 3.7 GB free VRAM for 60 FPS flight. No borrowing needed for daily work.
- **Optional Temporary Hardware Borrowing**: ASUS ROG Strix (8GB VRAM) / HP Victus (6GB VRAM) can be borrowed temporarily on final presentation day if heavy Unreal Engine cinematics are requested.
- **Ground Control & Telemetry Node**: **MacBook**. Runs React + Mapbox GL JS 3D GCS dashboard, QGroundControl, and Foxglove Studio telemetry.

### 🛡️ Rule 003: Document Formatting & PDF Generation
- **Theme Preference**: Light theme by default for team execution documents with clear daily goals and milestones.
- **Visuals**: Always include high-resolution generated visual assets (Gemini images), SVG flowcharts, and clear color-coded role badges.
- **Page Budget**: Always budget page heights cleanly (`height: 277mm`) to ensure EXACT page counts with ZERO trailing blank pages.

### 🛡️ Rule 004: Token-Efficient MCP Building Super-Stack & Memory Policy
- **Memory Persistence Policy**: **AVOID `agentmemory` MCP tool.** Use `contextm` / file-backed persistent rules (`.cursorrules`, `SKILL.md`, `docs/`) for persistent context memory across turns.
- **Code Graphing & AST Queries**: Always use `code-review-graph` MCP server tools (`get_minimal_context_tool`, `semantic_search_nodes_tool`, `get_impact_radius_tool`) for minimal context token usage.
- **Task Offloading**: Use `opencode-offloader` MCP server tools (`opencode_quick_edit`, `opencode_run_task`) to offload routine refactoring, boilerplate code generation, and unit test scaffolding to background fast models.
- **Targeted File Inspection**: Always specify exact `StartLine` / `EndLine` ranges when calling `view_file` to keep context windows minimal.

### 🛡️ Rule 005: GitHub Monorepo Architecture Standard
- **Single Repository**: The entire team MUST work within a single GitHub monorepo (`https://github.com/Team-Offgrid/SUTRA.git`).
- **Workspace Layout**:
  ```
  SUTRA/
  ├── sutra_ws/src/sutra_gnc/          # Subsystem A (Rohith)
  ├── sutra_ws/src/sutra_comms/        # Subsystem B (Nikhil)
  ├── sutra_ws/src/sutra_perception/   # Subsystem C (Vedanth)
  ├── sutra_ws/src/sutra_gcs/          # Subsystem D (Siva Kesava)
  ├── sutra_ws/src/sutra_sim/          # Subsystem B & E (Sim / Harika)
  └── docs/                            # Subsystem E (Harika)
  ```
- **Branch Strategy**: Protected `main`, integration `dev`, and individual feature branches (`feature/subsystem-a-gnc`, `feature/subsystem-b-comms`, `feature/subsystem-c-perception`, `feature/subsystem-d-gcs`, `feature/subsystem-e-docs`).
